== P5 the affine-regular pentagon in Q(sqrt5): v_{k+1} = (1/phi) v_k - v_{k-1}
PASS P5.0 recurrence closes: v5 = v0, and the vertices sum to 0 (centroid 0 by D5 symmetry below)
PASS P5.0b convex, counterclockwise: every consecutive cross product is positive
PASS P5.1 R permutes the vertices as the 5-cycle [1, 2, 3, 4, 0]; S as the reflection [0, 4, 3, 2, 1]
PASS P5.2 the generated group has order 10 (D5)
PASS P5.3 frames (perfectly distinguishable ordered vertex pairs) = the 10 ordered distance-2 pairs: [(0, 2), (0, 3), (1, 3), (1, 4), (2, 0), (2, 4), (3, 0), (3, 1), (4, 1), (4, 2)]
PASS P5.4 each frame has an explicit effect: 1 on the first vertex, 0 on the second, in [0,1] on every vertex
PASS P5.5 countercontrol: the adjacent pair (v0, v1) is not a frame (normal cones of v0 and -v1 do not meet)
PASS P5.6 capacity two: no three pairwise-distinguishable vertices (triples: []); capacity >= 2: a frame exists
PASS P5.7 SS: the D5-orbit of the ordered frame (v0, v2) has 10 elements = all ordered frames
PASS P5.8 the theorem's mechanism: no frame has the centroid as midpoint
PASS P5.9 Spec2 fails: the centroid lies on no frame segment (not even on a frame line)
PASS P5.10 BP fails: the edge midpoint (v0+v1)/2 attains the max of the edge-0 functional (a proper effect is certain there, KF:227) and is a proper midpoint, so it is a non-extreme boundary state
PASS P5.11 ELEM2: the midpoint of the frame (v0, v2) is an interior point
PASS P5.12 the form Q = [[1, 1/(2phi)], [1/(2phi), 1]] is D5-invariant (R^T Q R = Q and S^T Q S = Q)
PASS P5.13 Q is positive definite (q11 > 0, det > 0)
PASS P5.14 one alpha = (1/4+1/4*r5) makes M(1, v_(k+3)) orthogonal to both generators (1, v_k), (1, v_(k+1)) of facet k, for every k
PASS P5.15 strong self-duality: M = diag(alpha, Q) is positive definite and D5-invariant, M(1, v_j) pairs nonnegatively with every generator and vanishes on exactly the two generators of the opposite facet; so M maps the 5 extreme rays of K onto the 5 extreme rays of K*, K* = M K
== harness controls: square and affine-regular hexagon
PASS H.1 square: every ordered pair of distinct vertices is a frame (12 = 12)
PASS H.2 hexagon: 18 ordered frames, each vertex with its two distance-2 and its opposite vertex (18)
PASS H.3 D6 generators act on the hexagon: [[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 0], [2, 1, 0, 5, 4, 3]]
PASS H.4 SS fails for the hexagon: 2 orbits of sizes [6, 12]; each orbit is uniform in 'midpoint = centroid' (the theorem's invariant separates them)
PASS H.5 strong self-duality test rejects the square: no D4-invariant diag(alpha, lambda I) maps a generator to a facet normal (no generator has equal negative pairings with two adjacent generators)
== BD the bidisk D x D = conv(S1 x S1) in R^4 (the torus orbitope)
PASS BD.1 both pairs are frames: explicit effects (|a1|+|a2| = 1/2) give 1 on the first and 0 on the second member
PASS BD.2 SS fails: midpoint(f1) = ((Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(0, 1)), (Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(0, 1))) is the centroid 0, midpoint(f2) = ((Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(0, 1)), (Fraction(1, 1), Fraction(0, 1))) is not; every affine automorphism fixes the centroid (TB:356), so none maps f1 to f2
PASS BD.3 the frame members are extreme points (both components unit vectors); capacity two by central symmetry about 0 (Lemma D, KF:632, written)
PASS BD.4 BP fails: ((1,0),(0,0)) is certain for the proper effect e2 (so a boundary state) and is the midpoint of the distinct states ((1,0),(1,0)) and ((1,0),(-1,0))
PASS BD.5 Spec2 holds on 43 exact rational samples (B <= A, the written construction: x2 = v, y2 = -v, p = (1+B)/2, unit x1, y1 solving p x1 + (1-p) y1 = A u); each decomposition is along a frame (y2 = -x2)
== ST the Stiefel orbitope conv V2(R^3) = {X in R^(3x2) : ||X||_op <= 1}
PASS ST.1 (A, -A) and (A, B) are frames of extreme points (orthonormal columns): the effect (1 + X_11)/2 is 1 on A, 0 on -A and on B
PASS ST.2 SS fails: midpoint(A,-A) = 0 = centroid, midpoint(A,B) = ((Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(0, 1)), (Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(1, 1)), (Fraction(0, 1), Fraction(0, 1))) != 0
PASS ST.3 BP fails: [e1, 0] is certain for (1 + X_11)/2 (proper) and is the midpoint of [e1, e2] and [e1, -e2]
PASS ST.4 Spec2 exact instance: X = [[1/2, 0], [0, 1/4], [0, 0]] is p A + (1-p) B with A, B in V2 and A e2 = -B e2 (a frame)
== Q3 the qutrit: frames are orthonormal triples
PASS Q3.1 BP fails: diag(1/2,1/2,0) is certain for the proper effect diag(1,1,0) and is the midpoint of |0><0| and |1><1|
PASS Q3.2 Spec (triples) instance: a rational orthonormal basis and weights give a state that is a mixture of a perfectly distinguishable triple; the triple's projectors sum to 1
PASS Q3.3 SS (triples) instance: the orthogonal (so unitary) U, U^T U = 1, maps the ordered standard frame (e0, e1, e2) to the ordered frame of its columns
PASS Q3.4 capacity three: the diagonal projectors sum to 1 and tr(P_k |j><j|) = delta_kj
== M the Bloch ball (positive control for the mechanism)
PASS M.1 SS witness: a rational rotation (det +1, orthogonal) maps the ordered frame (e3, -e3) to (n, -n), n = (2/3, 1/3, 2/3)
PASS M.2 Spec2 on the ball: each sample x = t n is ((1+t)/2) n + ((1-t)/2)(-n), an antipodal frame
PASS M.3 mechanism: every antipodal frame has midpoint 0 = centroid; BP holds on the ball (strictly convex; kernel singletonFaces_closedBall KF:658)
== C2 the Caratheodory orbitope conv{(cos t, sin t, cos 2t, sin 2t)}: capacity three, BP fails
PASS C2.1 capacity >= 3: three affine functionals with E_i(gamma(t_j)) = delta_ij, sum = 1 identically, and E_i(gamma(t)) = (4/9)(1-cos(t-t_j))(1-cos(t-t_k)) >= 0 on the curve (hence effects on the hull)
PASS C2.2 BP fails: E_0 vanishes at gamma(t_1) and gamma(t_2), so their midpoint is certain for the effect E_1 + E_2 = 1 - E_0, which is proper (value 0 at gamma(t_0)); the midpoint of two distinct points is not extreme
c3_bp: 40/40 checks pass
VERDICT BP-SPEC-SS: the controls hold; Spec2 + SS (+ capacity two) give BP and pure-state transitivity (written Theorem BP-S); each premise and the capacity-two scope are load-bearing: pentagon (SS, self-dual, cap 2; no Spec2, no BP), bidisk and Stiefel (Spec2, cap 2; no SS, no BP), qutrit (Spec, SS with triples; no BP), Caratheodory (cap >= 3; no BP)
